INT. LIGHTHOUSE FOG-SIGNAL ROOM - NIGHT

The brass horn sits silent. Rain ticks on the glass. IGNATIUS BRAND (60s, salt-cracked hands, wool cap) pours tea for TAMSIN OKORO (20s, relief keeper, soaked parka).

TAMSIN
Quiet night.

IGNATIUS
Always is, after the horn stops.

They sip. The kettle ticks as it cools. Tamsin smiles.

TAMSIN
Thought it'd be worse out here.

Ignatius stares at the floor between her boots. Water pools there. Too much water, and it runs uphill toward the horn.

IGNATIUS
(barely a whisper)
You came up alone?

TAMSIN
Yes. Why?

Below them, slow wet footsteps climb the iron stairs. Tamsin and Ignatius both freeze, cups halfway to their mouths.

The horn BLARES on its own. They scramble for the hatch, collide, and drag it shut together.

IGNATIUS
That's not the tide.
